1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,744
A wind from the Sun hits Earth at about four hundred kilometers per second.

2
00:00:04,744 --> 00:00:07,439
An invisible magnetic shield pushes it away.

3
00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:09,653
What if that shield switched off?

4
00:00:09,653 --> 00:00:12,182
Every compass on Earth would stop pointing north.

5
00:00:12,683 --> 00:00:14,965
Surprisingly, you'd mostly be fine.

6
00:00:14,965 --> 00:00:18,029
The air above you is the real radiation shield.

7
00:00:18,517 --> 00:00:22,653
But satellites and astronauts would be exposed to every blast from the Sun.

8
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:26,784
And big solar storms could eat into the ozone layer for years.

9
00:00:27,283 --> 00:00:28,885
Forty-one thousand years ago,

10
00:00:28,885 --> 00:00:32,642
the field really did drop to about five percent of today's strength.

11
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:34,551
Full story on the channel.
